Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:28:16 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 06/22] qwen3_5: the mHC router routes 16/S rows a block,
 reading its weights and each row once

One block per row re-read the 256 KiB fp32 router matrix for every row and the row's streams nine times.
A block now takes 8 rows at two streams: each thread reads a weight column once for all its rows, keeps the
square sum beside the dots, and the row norm scales the dots after. Prefill at 8k: 1934 -> 2048 tok/s (q4,
GB10); router time 537 -> 174 ms. BF16 step and prompt logits are bit-identical to the previous kernel.
